<details {{ $attributes->class(['mb-3']) }}>
  <summary class="py-2" style="min-height:44px;cursor:pointer">How your rating works</summary>
  <div class="mt-2" style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">
    <p>Your Cape Tennis rating estimates your playing strength on a <strong>0–100 scale: higher means stronger</strong>. It is separate from your tournament position or ranking.</p>
    <ul class="ps-3">
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Who you play matters.</strong> Results are assessed against your opponents’ strength, rather than awarding fixed points for each win.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Scores matter too.</strong> A convincing win generally provides stronger evidence than a narrow win, with limits on how much the score margin can influence the calculation.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Recent results count more.</strong> We use eligible results from the past two years. A result’s weight halves approximately every six months (180 days).</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>One event has limited influence.</strong> Playing many matches at one tournament cannot overwhelm results from other events.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>You carry one shared rating across age groups.</strong> Entering a new age group does not reset it. Age, gender and finishing positions do not automatically add or subtract rating points.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Only eligible played standard-singles results count.</strong> Doubles, byes, walkovers and results with unresolved player identities or invalid scores are excluded. Modified-ball or reduced-court tennis is kept separate. Some older conventional age categories use an assumed standard playing format; these are identified in the evidence.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your <strong>confidence indicator</strong> describes the supporting evidence, not an accuracy percentage. Sparse, older or poorly connected results mean lower confidence. Shared ratings are comparable only between players connected to the same reference group; players without sufficient connecting evidence may remain unrated.</p>
    <p>Ratings can change when new results are added, opponents play, older results lose weight, or scores are corrected—even when you have not recently played. Separate historical age-context estimates, where shown, apply only within their own group.</p>
    <p class="mb-0"><strong>A rating is a provisional estimate, not a guaranteed match prediction or an official selection decision.</strong> It is local to Cape Tennis and is not a conversion to UTR or World Tennis Number.</p>
  </div>
</details>
